    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0813" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4R1/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-19T17:00:00+01:00">June 19, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 19—1:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>84. I am in receipt of invitation from Secretary General of League of Nations,
                    dated June 18, to the American Government to participate in a conference in
                    Bangkok, Siam, to open November 9, 1931, to discuss position in regard to
                    chapter II of the Hague Convention<anchor n="21" xml:id="d538-f1"/> and
                    application of the Geneva Agreement<anchor n="22" xml:id="d538-f2"/> on the
                    basis of the report to [<hi rendition="#italic">of</hi>] the Commission of
                    Inquiry into the Control of Opium Smoking in the Far East.<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d538-f3"/> The United States and China are included in this
                    invitation in accordance with a resolution of the Council adopted May 23
                        last.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d538-f4"/> Mailing invitation today by
                        pouch.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d538-f5"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="21" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p>Signed January 23, 1912, <ref target="frus1912#pg_196"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foreign Relations</hi>, 1912, p. 196</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f2" n="22" xml:id="d538-f2-content">
                <p>Signed February 11, 1925, by the British Empire (with India), China, France,
                    Japan, the Netherlands, Portugal, and Siam; League of Nations Treaty Series,
                    vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">li</hi>, p. 337.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f3" n="23" xml:id="d538-f3-content">
                <p>League of Nations document C.635.M.254.1930.XI. (Geneva, November, 1930).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f4" n="24" xml:id="d538-f4-content">
                <p>See League of Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Sixty-third Session of the
                        Council:</hi> Minutes of the Sixth Meeting (Council/63rd Session/P. V. 6
                    (1)), p. 3.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f5" n="25" xml:id="d538-f5-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
